WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.640
So some of you may have noticed that there's

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.660
a problem with YouTube today.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.100
And I'm not just talking about

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.500
"Oh, YouTube should listen to its creators more.."

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.080
"Oh, they should do this or that differently..."

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.900
I am talking about a fundamental problem

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.560
with the website itself.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.260
And this isn't just about me.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.720
I'm not making this video because I think that I'M being unfairly treated

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:19.860
in any way, shape, or form.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.260
If anything, I am in a really good position

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.580
but this is affecting a lot of people

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.200
and I think the reason for it needs to be brought into light.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.100
Now, if you are paying attention to YouTube,

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.820
you probably noticed that last week

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:34.320
last Tuesday on October 16, the website went down.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.120
Worldwide for 2 hours, it went down.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.020
Which has never really happened in YouTube before..

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.800
and a lot of people wanted to know "why?"

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.220
But I have a sneaking suspicion that I know EXACTLY why..

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.320
and it all comes down to 1 culprit.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.400
Google+.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.560
And I'm not just using Google+ as a "scapegoat"

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.100
and it's easy to do that because it's a terrible thing

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.520
that was forced on.. ALL of YouTube

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.520
for no particular reason other than "Google wanted to."

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.200
To give you a little history on Google+

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.280
and why it's so deeply ingrained in Youtube..

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.480
you have to go back to 2014 when Google decided

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.540
that it was going to be manditory

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.840
for creators on YouTube to GET a Google+ account.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.020
You had to tie your YouTube channel INTO Google+

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:16.800
no matter what.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.400
It didn't matter if the service was good, or that they cared about natural growth.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.320
They wanted to force it down people's throats

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.400
so that they could have a Facebook competator.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.180
Now, this isn't about the morals or Google+ being integrated into YouTube

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.560
That's not what this video is about

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.980
and frankly, I'm not the best to even argue about that.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.000
I'm telling you this to emphasize

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.820
how deep this really went.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.880
To see how much of YouTube

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.320
had Google+ embedded inside of it.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:44.520
It came down to every single programmer being

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.740
incentivized to integrate Google+ as much as they could.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.420
They had BONUSES implemented into Google+

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.060
so that programmers would be rewarded the more

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.860
they were able to force it into YouTube's code.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.280
And.. with that in mind, that leads into TODAY.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.900
Because, before the crash on YouTube

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.600
on October 8, I believe,

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.580
it was announced that Google+ was shutting down completely

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:09.820
because of some embarrassing privacy leaks.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:11.960
Google didn't want to be exposed to irregulations, so

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.800
they shut it down completely to try to avoid any fanfare about it.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.880
And in doing so, they have fundamentally crippled YouTube.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:25.400
So, Google+ isn't dead YET, but it has started the process of shutting down.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.180
As they are shutting down Google+,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.720
it is breaking more and more thing inside of YouTube.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.460
And these things are still broken, and they're getting worse

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.640
Now, now, it's almost a meme at this point

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.260
that people are like "My videos aren't going out to sub-boxes!"

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.480
But now, it's actually a problem.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.820
Across the board, a lot of YouTubers are seeing a 30 to 40% dip

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:48.240
in the number of initial viewers and prolonged viewers,

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:50.780
suggested videos aren't working properly,

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.340
people aren't getting their notifications properly.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.200
There's a lot of different recipes that are causing problems.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.380
It's not enough that it's completely broken

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.480
but it's enough to create a noticeable difference

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:04.780
and an impact on the bottom line of a lot of YouTuber's.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.060
Just to show you how deep this actually goes

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.560
if I go into my channel here

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.560
This is- This is basically my channel

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:15.080
The back-end of my Creator Studio where I manage all videos

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:19.280
There are certain pages in here that just don't actually work.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.640
If I click on these pages in here

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.400
some of them take up to a minute to load

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:23.900
*NO!*

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.900
Some don't load at all... They just break

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.560
And I've told them about this, and they still haven't gotten back to me

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.560
And I think the reason is...

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.120
is because they don't know how to fix it.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.460
And I think that's the main problem with YouTube right now

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.660
The problem is so big

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.280
because Google+ was so deeply integrated into YouTube

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.440
They have no idea how to separate it out at this point

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.580
So here's my guess in what happened...

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.500
They pushed a code change on Tuesday

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.540
that caused all of YouTube to crash.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.860
They reverted the change

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.720
And now they're trying to analyze exactly what happened

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.720
And because it's so big

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.760
they're gonna be very slow about it

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.480
And the worst thing about it

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.160
is that this wouldn't be nearly as big a problem

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:11.260
If YouTube actually communicated that there was a problem

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.360
You can't just pretend that there's nothing wrong on the platform

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.860
For people like me,

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.540
those who are high up on the platform

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:21.560
I don't really have a problem with it because I can weather these issues month to month

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.400
But there's a lot of creators out there

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.240
That can't...

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:26.960
That really rely on this on a day to day basis

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.740
And as much as this is a fun job to have-

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.060
As much as it's cool to entertain people

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:35.000
There are people that now, like, rely on this.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.900
Rely on the consistency of it.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.560
The sad truth is that we are called partners with YouTube, but we are not partners.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.940
We're less than employes

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.820
YouTube doesn't actually care about it's creators-

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.280
And I'm not saying that in a very... like-

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.900
"Ah. The worlds ended. YouTube doesn't are about us"

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.500
They legitimately don't...

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:54.920
Because they can't

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:58.140
Or at least they don't have the the system in place to do so

00:04:58.320 --> 00:04:59.600
They can want it...

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.100
They can hope for it...

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:06.840
But until they put the system in place that actually gives benefits towards its creators,

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.320
nothing's gonna change

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:09.760
People are still gonna suffer

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.100
There's still gonna be this negative attitude towards YouTube

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.620
because they rely on code and algorithm

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:20.820
As opposed to real people, interacting with the real people who are making content on this platform

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:27.300
And until they treat the humans that are making the content with humans that are supporting the content

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:28.560
It'll never work

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.560
I might be wrong about the specific reason,

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:33.460
but that doesn't change the fact that there is a problem with Youtube.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:35.420
And it doesn't change the fact that

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:37.420
Youtube won't tell us that there is a problem

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.500
If Youtube is going to be a place where creators can thrive,

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:43.000
and people can whatever content they want,

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.700
then you got to start treating us like people,

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:46.240
all of us.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:49.540
If we really matter... show us that we matter.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.080
and even for someone like me,

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.820
who gets preferential treatment on these things,

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:55.760
i'm still kept in the dark about it.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:02.780
I have to tell them about the problems with their own platform, that they refuse to respond to me about.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:04.980
and if they treat me this way,

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.080
what do they do to people who have less subsribers than me?

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:09.360
It's not ok.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.280
It's really, honestly, truly ,not ok.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:15.400
They've shoved Google+ down the throats of everybody on this platform,

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:19.720
and now people are suffering from it, because they don't see this platform

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:25.720
as a place for creativity to thrive, they see it as a tool to push their agenda.

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:30.980
and that's fine, they own it, it's their right, but we helped build it.

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:35.500
so anyway, let me know down in the comments if you've seen other issues with the platform,

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.660
if you've seen other issues on YouTube. Try to keep it not so much about the morals of it,

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.500
and try to keep it down to the technical issues that are happening right now.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.740
We've got technical problems, that need technical answers.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:48.180
communication is an issue, and hopefully that'll get fixed soon.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.860
But for right now, let's try to fix the problem.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:55.600
So, thank you everybody for watching, and as alyways see you in the next one. buh-bye.

